{
  "decision": "map_front",
  "rationale": "The feasible front is confined to a narrow slice of both objectives: area_um2 6997..10027 and accuracy_bits 10.6..11.6, while the registry allows data_width up to 28 and n_iter up to 30, so much higher accuracy is reachable. With the HV area reference at 40000, the (40000-area) factor is ~33000 for every front point, so extending accuracy_bits upward adds large HV rectangles; the current front stops at 11.55 bits. The throughput constraint is already trivially satisfied (best seen 14.8 MSPS vs >=1), and the summary reports no unexplored families, so pipelined/pipelined_m cannot help the min-area objective (same accuracy bits at strictly more registers). The remaining 100 evals are therefore best spent letting NSGA-II map the full ranges of the two families already on the front (iterative, unrolled_k), seeded with the current front, to cover the accuracy dimension and any lower-area corner before the final min-area selection."
  ,
  "next_plan": null
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Budget is exhausted (200/200 evals) and this is the final round, so only stop/infeasible apply. Infeasible is ruled out: 125 of 200 evaluations are feasible, 0% violate throughput_msps >= 1 (best 14.8 vs. required 1), and the accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 0.000976562 is achievable with huge margin (best 4.35e-08 = 2^-24.45; even the selected design's 6.42e-04 passes). The Pareto front is well covered over the region that matters for the spec: area_um2 spans 6997..15084 against the HV reference of 40000, and accuracy_bits spans 10.6..24.5 against the HV reference of 10, with data_width 15..28 on the front. Hypervolume is still improving (+17.4% this round to 4.168e+05), but with no further evaluations available there is nothing more to gain. Under the selection rule (min area_um2), the pick is the iterative design [data_width=15, n_iter=13, angle_guard=2, frac_guard=0, rounding=round]: area_um2=6997, accuracy_bits=10.6 (max_abs_err=0.000642, satisfying the <=2^-10 limit), throughput 8.5 MSPS (>= 1 MSPS), 101 FFs, power_index 0.155."
  , "next_plan": null
}
